🔹 What is ScrollPosition in JPA?

Spring Data introduced:

ScrollPosition
Window<T>

👉 This is cursor-based pagination built into Spring Data JPA

So instead of manually passing cursor=id, you use:

ScrollPosition
🔹 1. Repository Implementation
public interface UserRepository extends JpaRepository<User, Long> {

    Window<User> findAllByOrderByIdAsc(ScrollPosition position, Pageable pageable);

}
🔹 2. Service Layer
public Window<User> getUsers(ScrollPosition position) {

    Pageable limit = PageRequest.ofSize(10);

    if (position == null) {
        position = ScrollPosition.keyset(); // start
    }

    return userRepository.findAllByOrderByIdAsc(position, limit);
}
🔹 3. Controller
@GetMapping("/users")
public Map<String, Object> getUsers(
        @RequestParam(required = false) String cursor) {

    ScrollPosition position = (cursor == null)
            ? ScrollPosition.keyset()
            : ScrollPosition.of(cursor);

    Window<User> window = userService.getUsers(position);

    String nextCursor = window.positionAt(window.size() - 1).toString();

    return Map.of(
        "data", window.getContent(),
        "nextCursor", nextCursor
    );
}
🔹 4. How Scroll Position Works Internally

Instead of:

OFFSET 100

It does:

WHERE id > last_seen_id

👉 But Spring handles this internally using keyset pagination

🔹 5. Types of ScrollPosition
✅ Keyset (Recommended)
ScrollPosition.keyset()
Uses indexed fields
Fast
No duplicates
❌ Offset (Avoid for large data)
ScrollPosition.offset()
Same as LIMIT OFFSET
Slow for big tables
🔹 6. Important Rules 🚀
✅ You MUST:
Have ORDER BY in method name
findAllByOrderByIdAsc(...)
✅ Use indexed column
id OR createdAt
⚠️ For real-world (better sorting)
findAllByOrderByCreatedAtAscIdAsc(...)
🔹 7. Interview Answer (Perfect 🔥)

If asked:

👉 “How do you implement scroll position in JPA?”

You say:

Spring Data JPA provides ScrollPosition and Window<T> for keyset pagination.
It avoids OFFSET and uses indexed columns to fetch next records efficiently.
We pass the scroll position (cursor) and get the next window of data.

🔹 8. Difference vs Manual Cursor
| Approach               | Complexity | Control           |
| ---------------------- | ---------- | ----------------- |
| Manual (`id > cursor`) | Medium     | Full control      |
| `ScrollPosition`       | Easy       | Framework handles |

🔹 Final Summary
Scroll position = cursor internally
Use ScrollPosition.keyset()
Return Window<T>
Always use ORDER BY
Best for infinite scroll APIs